<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">County Cork</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">County <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cork">Cork</a> is the largest county in Ireland, in the south-west of the province of Munster, named after the city of Cork. Its west has a deeply indented coast and in early medieval times was home to kingdoms of the Corcu Loigde and branches of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eoganachta">Eóganachta</a>. The county was created after the Norman conquest.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/county-cork.jpg" alt="County Cork" width="320" height="400" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Island_of_Ireland_location_map.svg: *Ireland_location_map.svg: NordNordWest Northern_Ireland_location_map.svg: NordNo... · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Island_of_Ireland_location_map_Cork.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
